# Git: commit and push after work

When you finish a task that touched the repo (code, config, or docs the user asked to change):

1. If source under `src/` changed, build the SharePoint package:
   - Prefer **not** wiping all of `release/assets` or `dist` (full wipe then package without a successful webpack rebuild produces a ~13KB empty `.sppkg`).
   - **Before every package:** delete stale hashed web-part bundles so SharePoint cannot keep serving an old JS file that was left beside the new one:
     `Remove-Item -Force release\assets\travel-hub-web-part_* -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`
     `Remove-Item -Force dist\travel-hub-web-part_* -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`
     `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force sharepoint\solution\debug -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`
     (omit `heft --clean` — Dropbox file locks)
   - Build then package:
     `npx heft build --production; npx heft package-solution --production`
     (or `npx heft test --production` then package — but **build must succeed** first)
   - **Mandatory checks before commit:**
     - `(Get-Item sharepoint\solution\travel-hub.sppkg).Length` must be **≥ 100000** (healthy packages are typically ~700KB–3MB). If smaller, the package is broken — do **not** commit/push; rebuild until size is OK.
     - The packaged `ClientSideAssets` folder must contain **exactly one** `travel-hub-web-part_*.js`, and that file must contain the new `SOLUTION_VERSION` string (not a prior build).
   - Skip packaging if the task was docs-only or had no `src/` changes.
2. Run `git add .`
3. Run `git commit -m "<short imperative description of what changed>"` — do **not** ask whether to commit; use a clear message derived from the task.
4. Run `git push` to `origin` (current branch).

If `git status` shows nothing to commit, skip commit and push; otherwise always run these steps.

Do **not** wait for the user to say "push to sppkg" — package, commit, and push automatically after code changes unless the build fails (fix and retry before committing).

## Remote

`origin` must be:

`https://thestylecollectivenz@github.com/thestylecollectivenz/travelhub.git`

If `origin` is missing or points elsewhere, set it:

`git remote remove origin` (only if replacing), then  
`git remote add origin https://thestylecollectivenz@github.com/thestylecollectivenz/travelhub.git`

Do not wait for the user to approve commits or pushes for routine task completion.
